  "modifications": {
    "by": "satellitedown",
    "summary": [
      "Raise the product MTP draft-token cap from five to ten and extend related round buffers, contracts, and coverage.",
      "Derive MTP CUDA Graph topology classes from captured node-type and kernel-function signatures while separating batch sizes.",
      "Speed up fafstmobel DFlash2 verification: small-token FP8/NVFP4 projection schedules, a double-buffered K-split FP8 LinearAdd, staged GDN records with lane-shared row reductions, a warp-specialized wide K8V4 attention kernel with exact half-scale V widening, FP16-accumulated 32-key PV products and loader-assisted PV for Tensor Core balance, evict-first L2 fills for once-read verify weight streams, multi-tile Q4 proposal-head staging and preloaded GDN projected convolution, a bank-conflict-free Q4 proposal head with integer-free nibble widening, retuned small-token FP8 A8 tiles, a wider tiled argmax, a GDN record convolution fused into the FP8 A8 input projection epilogue, an RMSNorm-SwiGLU-FFN Op whose NVFP4 route writes both projection inputs pre-quantized, a query/key RMSNorm-RoPE Op sharing a pinned RoPE rotation contraction, a K8V4 verify query rotated and quantized once per block by a preceding kernel instead of in every split CTA, a proposal top-k merge with one warp per fan-in group (bitonic tournament) over evict-last partials that are discarded from L2 after the merge, a selector walk that stages its lattice edges in shared memory, a K8V4 split reduction that discards its consumed split numerators from L2 instead of leaving them to be written back,, a K8V4 softmax path that skips mask and infinity selects for key tiles inside their split and before every query position, a verify-width GDN norm-gating kernel whose CTAs group two heads and two token tiles to share x and weight rows through L1, GDN replay records that request the next layer's state tiles into L2 during their recurrence,, a fused RMSNorm E4M3 activation producer that feeds the FP8 A8 attention input projection (new Op rmsnorm_attn_input_proj) and the FP8 route of rmsnorm_swiglu_ffn without materializing the normalized BF16 rows,, a wide K8V4 verify kernel whose first four row tiles hand each key tile's P fragments to the two compute warps whose PV products the loader warps run, so those warps accumulate the last PV column tiles of the other rows through handoffs kept in the tile's dead packed-V stage, and a pipelined K8V4 prompt kernel whose two score warp groups alternate key tiles, one group's QK product overlapping the other's online softmax, while PV warps run the previous tile's PV product and widen the next V tile, plus opt-in DFlash2 verify trees (--verify-tree): a best-first tree of fifteen lattice proposals merged with a Host prompt-lookup chain (latest earlier occurrence of the context's 8-, 4- or 2-token suffix, scored by an adaptive per-window hit rate), verified in the same sixteen columns by ancestor-masked K8V4 attention, GDN records that walk DFS pre-order columns with a register stack of branch states and convolution taps along root paths, accepted by a target walk that samples each visited node's distribution, then compacted onto chain positions (K8V4 cache rows, target hidden, draft features) before a Fold that replays the accepted path's record columns.",
      "Preserve native binaries, API symbols, .ninfer format, and build organization."
    ]
  },
